          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://www.hedidntjump.com/#zioncheck-faq-1",
          "name": "Who was Marion Zioncheck?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Marion Zioncheck (Marion A. Zioncheck; also Marion Anthony Zioncheck) was a U.S. Representative and Seattle congressman from 1933 to 1936. Official reports said he died by suicide at the Arctic Building in Seattle on 7 August 1936. This archive publishes newspapers and five volumes that re-examine that official account."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
