            "text": "Contemporary official and press accounts said Seattle congressman Marion A. Zioncheck died by suicide from a fifth-floor Arctic Building office on 7 August 1936. He Didn't Jump publishes newspapers and five research volumes that re-examine that official suicide account. It does not invent court holdings or quotes beyond what those volumes and cited papers print."
